// What is written out about a view: the rectangles, the computed values, the text, the pixels. One line a node,
// the nodes numbered as tc_nodes numbers them, so a web page's elements in document order line up with them.
//
// One line per node: its number, its rectangle x y w h, and its kind (1 Row, 2 Col, 3 Text, ...).
tc_rects(int[] t, string[] s, int[] rc, int[] ns) {
  string[] ls = [];
  int i = 0;
  while (i < len(ns)) {
    push(ls, tc_rect1(t, rc, ns[i], i));
    i = i + 1;
  }
} chain (int[] t, string[] s, int[] rc, int[] ns) {
  string txt = str_join(ls, "\n") + "\n";
} return string txt;
given tc_t_view ((import tc_tt), (import tc_ts), (import tc_xr), (import tc_xn)):("0 0 0 60 40 2\n1 9 9 42 11 3\n2 9 24 42 9 2\n")
